 - 2026-06-11: CLOSED-LOOP GROUNDED REPLANNING over the vc33 verified WM (G2 -- is the search layer salvageable?): exp4035's open-loop search found a DEGENERATE plan that exploited a WM defect and failed in the real env. Replace open-loop planning with CLOSED-LOOP per-step grounding: (a) plan a short horizon over the verified WM (reuse exp4034's precision-1.0 goal predicate + the vc33 WM program), execute ONLY the first action in the REAL env, RE-OBSERVE the real state, replan from there (receding horizon / MPC); (b) a WM-TRUST/DIVERGENCE gate -- after each real step compare the WM-predicted next-state vs the REAL observed next-state; on divergence, distrust the WM locally and re-induce / fall back / abstain (this is what catches the degenerate [6,38,28]x70 exploit); (c) refuse degenerate plans (single-action-repeat that the WM claims reaches goal). REAL-ENV-CONFIRM any solve via level_completed. Honest no-solve is a COMPLETE verdict -- but it must DISTINGUISH 'closed-loop grounding broke the wall' from 'the verified-WM-as-simulator has a sim2real ceiling on vc33' (report the per-step WM<->real divergence rate). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: closed_loop_no_solve_vc33_wm_sim2real_ceiling_divergence_0.207; results/experiment_4046_closed_loop_replan_over_vc33_wm.json
